{
  "title": "80: Abasa عبس",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nعَبَسَ وَتَوَلّٰٓىۙ‏(1)\nA’BASA WA TAWALLAA.\nHe frowned and he turned away\nاَنْ جَآءَهُ الْاَعْمٰىؕ‏(2)\nAN JAAA-AHUL A-A’MAA.\nBecause came unto him the blind man\nوَمَا يُدْرِيْكَ لَعَلَّهٗ يَزَّكّٰٓىۙ‏(3)\nWA MAA YUDREEKA LA-A’LLAHU YAZZAKKAA.\nAnd what maketh thee to know that he would cleanse himself\nاَوْ يَذَّكَّرُ فَتَنْفَعَهُ الذِّكْرٰىؕ‏(4)\nAW YAZZAKKARO FATANFA-A’HUZ ZIKRAA.\nOr he warned, and profiteth him the warning?\nاَمَّا مَنِ اسْتَغْنٰىۙ‏(5)\nAMMAA MANIS TAGHNAA.\nAs for him who thinketh himself independent (on account of his wealth)\nفَاَنْتَ لَهٗ تَصَدّٰىؕ‏(6)\nFA-ANTA LAHU TASADDAA.\nUnto him dost thou attend\nوَمَا عَلَيْكَ اَلَّا يَزَّكّٰٓىؕ‏(7)\nWA MAA A’LAYKA ALLAA YAZZAKKAA.\nIt shall be no blame on thee if cleansed not himself\nوَاَمَّا مَنْ جَآءَكَ يَسْعٰىۙ‏(8)\nWA AMMAA MAN JAAA-A-KA YAS-A’A.\nBut as to him who cometh unto thee striving in earnest\nوَهُوَ يَخْشٰىۙ‏(9)\nWA HOWA YAKHSHAA.\nAnd feareth he (at heart)\nفَاَنْتَ عَنْهُ تَلَهّٰى‌ۚ‏(10)\nFA-ANTA A’NHO TALAHHAA.\nFrom him wilt thou be indifferent\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّهَا تَذْكِرَةٌ ۚ‏(11)\nKALLAA INNAHAA TAZKERAH.\nNay! but it (the Qur’an) is a reminder\nفَمَنْ شَآءَ ذَكَرَهٗ‌ۘ‏(12)\nFAMAN SHAA-A ZAKARAH.\nSo, let whosoever pleaseth, mind it\nفِىْ صُحُفٍ مُّكَرَّمَةٍۙ‏(13)\nFEE SOHOFIM MOKARRAMATIM.\n(It is written) in the Books greatly honoured.\nمَّرْفُوْعَةٍ مُّطَهَّرَةٍ ۭۙ‏(14)\nMARFOO-A’TIM MOTAHHARATIM.\nExalted high, purified\nبِاَيْدِىْ سَفَرَةٍۙ‏(15)\nBE-AYDEE SAFARATIN.\nIn the hands of the deputy angels\nكِرَامٍۢ بَرَرَةٍؕ‏(16)\nKERAAMIM BARARAH.\nNoble, virtuous\nقُتِلَ الْاِنْسَانُ مَاۤ اَكْفَرَهٗؕ‏(17)\nQOTELAL INSAANO MAA AKFARAH.\nCursed be man! How ungrateful is he?\nمِنْ اَىِّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقَهٗؕ‏(18)\nMIN  AYYE SHAY-IN KHALAQAH.\nOf” what thing did He create him?\nمِنْ نُّطْفَةٍؕ خَلَقَهٗ فَقَدَّرَهٗ ۙ‏(19)\nMIN NUTFAH, KHALAQAHU FAQADDARAHU.\nOf a Seminal - a drop; He created him, then fixed its measure\nثُمَّ السَّبِيْلَ يَسَّرَهٗۙ‏(20)\nSUMMAS SABEELA YASSARAHU.\n(And) then the way (for him) He made it easy\nثُمَّ اَمَاتَهٗ فَاَقْبَرَهٗۙ‏(21)\nSUMMA AMAATAHU FA-AQBARAHU.\nThen He causeth him to die, and got him buried\nثُمَّ اِذَا شَآءَ اَنْشَرَهٗؕ‏(22)\nSUMMA EZAA SHAA-A ANSHARAH.\nThen, when He willeth, He will again raise him (to life)\nكَلَّا لَمَّا يَقْضِ مَاۤ اَمَرَهٗؕ‏(23)\nKALLAA LAMMAA YAQZE MAA AMARAH.\nNay! he hath fulfilled not what He bade him\nفَلْيَنْظُرِ الْاِنْسَانُ اِلٰى طَعَامِهٖۤۙ‏(24)\nFAL-YANZORIL INSAANO ELAA TA-A’AMEH.\nThen, let man look at his food\nاَنَّا صَبَبْنَا الْمَآءَ صَبًّا ۙ‏(25)\nANNAA SABABNAL MAAA-A SABBAA.\nThat it was We Who poured down water in an abundant pouring\nثُمَّ شَقَقْنَا الْاَرْضَ شَقًّا ۙ‏(26)\nSUMMA SHAQAQNAN ARZA SHAQQAA.\nThen We cleft the earth, with a (necessary) cleaving\nفَاَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا حَبًّا ۙ‏(27)\nFA-ANBATNAA FEEHAA HABBANW.\nAnd caused We to grow’ therein the grain\nوَّ عِنَبًا وَّقَضْبًا ۙ‏(28)\nWA E’NABANW WA QAZBANW.\nAnd grapes and the vegetables\nوَّزَيْتُوْنًا وَّنَخْلًا ؕ‏(29)\nWA ZAYTOONANW WA NAKHLANW.\nThe Olive and the Palm\nوَحَدَآئِقَ غُلْبًا ۙ‏(30)\nWA HADAAA-EQA GULBANW.\nAnd gardens enclosed, thick with trees\nوَّفَاكِهَةً وَّاَبًّا ۙ‏(31)\nWA FAAKEHATNW WA ABBAM.\nAnd fruits and the herbage\nمَّتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِاَنْعَامِكُمْؕ‏(32)\nMATAA-A’L LAKUM WA LE-ANA’AMEKUM.\nA provision for you and your cattle\nفَاِذَا جَآءَتِ الصَّآخَّةُ‏(33)\nFE-EZAA JAAA-ATIS SAAAKHKHAH.\nBut when cometh the deafening Trumpet Blast\nيَوْمَ يَفِرُّ الْمَرْءُ مِنْ اَخِيْهِۙ‏(34)\nYAWMA YAFIRRUL MAR-O MIN AKHEEHE.\nThat day man will fly from his (own) brother\nوَاُمِّهٖ وَاَبِيْهِۙ‏(35)\nWA UMMEHI WA ABEEHE.\nAnd (from) his mother and (from) his father\nوَصَاحِبَتِهٖ وَبَنِيْهِؕ‏(36)\nWA SAAHEBATEHI WA BANEEHE.\nAnd (from) his wife and (his) children\nلِكُلِّ امْرِیءٍ مِّنْهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ شَاْنٌ يُّغْنِيْهِؕ‏(37)\nLEKULLIM RE-IM MINHUM YAWMA-EZIN SHAA-NUY YUGHNEEH.\nFor every man of them on that day will have a concern enough to make him heedless (of others)\nوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ مُّسْفِرَةٌ ۙ‏(38)\nWOJOOHINY YAWMA-EZIM MUSFERATUN.\n(there shall be) faces on that day radiant\nضَاحِكَةٌ مُّسْتَبْشِرَةٌ ۚ‏(39)\nZAAHEKATUM MUSTABSHERAH.\nLaughing, joyous\nوَوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ عَلَيْهَا غَبَرَةٌ ۙ‏(40)\nWA WOJOOHINY YAWMA-EZIN A’LAYHAA GHABARATUN.\nAnd (there shall be) faces on that day on them shall be dust\nتَرْهَقُهَا قَتَرَةٌ ؕ‏(41)\nTARHAQOHAA QATARAH.\nDarkness shall cover them\nاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْكَفَرَةُ الْفَجَرَةُ‏(42)\nOOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KAFARATUL FAJARAH.\nThese are they who are the disbelievers, the wicked",
  "merits": "Surah Abasa (He Frowned)\nThis Surah has 42 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the person who recites this Surah will come out of his grave laughing on the Day of Resurrection.\nWriting this Surah as a talisman on deerskin and keeping it in one’s possession makes one successful in all his endeavours. If it is recited during a journey, then the traveller will return home safely. Whoever recites this Surah with [Surah at-Takweer](A85) will be under the shade of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) in Jannah."
